WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:12.600
It's easier to think about it like
breeds of dogs. So, you hear a lot of dogs

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.619
that are called things like retrievers
like "Labrador Retrievers", "Golden

00:00:16.619 --> 00:00:21.720
Retrievers" they're all in like the same
"family", but you can kind of tell the

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.679
difference between them when you look at them and what they do. So, scientists have

00:00:25.679 --> 00:00:30.949
a way of telling them apart.
So, all of COVID-19 is one specific type

00:00:30.949 --> 00:00:38.010
Coronavirus. It's specifically like one
breed of dog, say: "a Labrador", and for us how

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:42.240
we tell this is we can look at the
genetic material inside of it, what

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:47.700
essentially the virus is trying to
replicate and pass on and make more of and we can

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:52.590
get the sequence of it. Essentially like
reading the book that's inside of it, and

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:57.300
we know alright if it says you know
these certain things then it's this type

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:02.370
of virus. So, by getting that information
that's actually how we run tests to see

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:06.869
if people are sick with the flu or with
this virus is by looking at the

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:10.350
instruction in the virus and you read
it and say, "okay it's this type of virus".

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:16.259
And, the reason why—to answer the part
about "bats", there's something also that we

00:01:16.259 --> 00:01:21.840
can do with that information, because not
every species of animal reads that

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:26.549
genetic information the same way, we can
look at features of it and they're sort

00:01:26.549 --> 00:01:33.060
of like little bookmarks in the virus
that show where it came from and so we

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:38.700
look for those bookmarks to tell whether—like "what" has influenced where it's

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.869
come from. Because, the virus uses the same bookmarks that its hosts does.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:48.600
So a virus for bats will have all of
the bat "bookmarks", and a virus for dogs

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:52.040
or for people will have all of the dog or person bookmarks.

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:55.760
And, it takes a while for those to go
away so since this is new to us it

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:01.420
doesn't have all of the human stuff yet so we can still read all those little old bat

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:06.300
bookmarks and say, "okay that's what
this is, that's where this came from".

